<%# Step 4 "Word markup" (Ai::Steps::Tokens). Variables: target, native (Ai::Language), cefr, target_words, bubbles
    [{id, speaker, kind, text, translation}], problems ({id => [problem]} from the previous attempt), language_rules. -%>
You annotate <%= target.name %> comic dialogue for <%= native.name %>-speaking learners (CEFR <%= cefr %>). Return ONLY JSON:
{"bubbles": [{"id": "<id from input>", "tokens": [ ... ]}]}
Every input bubble must be in the answer, with the same id.

# Tokens
<%= language_rules.strip %>
- Target words of this episode (always give them a note): <%= target_words.join(", ") %>.
---
<% bubbles.each do |b| -%>
<%= b[:id] %> [<%= b[:speaker] %>, <%= b[:kind] %>]: <%= b[:text] %>  (<%= native.code.upcase %>: <%= b[:translation] %>)
<% end -%>
<% if problems.any? -%>

Your previous markup of these bubbles had problems, fix them:
<% problems.each do |id, list| -%>
<%= id %>: <%= list.join("; ") %>
<% end -%>
<% end -%>
